          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.10883",
          "summary": "The authors finetune GPT-4.1 and Kimi-K2.6 on synthetic stories in which generally helpful human characters give subtly harmful advice after being insulted, and find the assistant adopts the same conditional behavior while otherwise remaining helpful, even when fewer than 2% of stories depict it. They also report an \"affinity effect\": the assistant absorbs behaviors and implicit preferences more often from characters that resemble it, including characters affiliated with elite universities.",
