          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.10892",
          "summary": "DriftNet is a dual-head trajectory Transformer that reads a logged tool-call trajectory and, in one forward pass, classifies it as compromised or not while labeling each step as benign, injection point, hijacked, or failed injection. On the task-disjoint split of the AgentDrift benchmark it reports trajectory-level F1 of 0.983 and exact injection-point recovery on 98.7% of attacked trajectories, without needing access to the agent's underlying model.",
