          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.11997",
          "summary": "DCRA is a training framework that repurposes the forward diffusion process as a structured corruption scheduler and adds a feature-level consistency objective that aligns representations across noise levels while preserving class-discriminative structure. It is encoder-agnostic, and in seizure detection experiments on the CHB-MIT EEG dataset it improves performance under multiple noise conditions and achieves higher sensitivity at low false-positive rates.",
